# Docs and ADRs

Docs and ADRs are part of the change. If you change behaviour, topology, deploy
path, substituters, auth, or a freeze: update the matching `docs/services/` /
runbook / README, add or amend an ADR under `docs/adr/` (ISO date + slug,
**one decision**, [MADR 3.0](docs/adr/2026-09-06-use-madr.md)), and put a
row under the matching topic in [docs/adr/README.md](docs/adr/README.md).

Do not leave the tree contradicting `docs/standards.md` or the README.

Closed coding slips belong in `docs/todo-deviations.md`; product and topology
freezes belong in ADRs. Current map (by topic):
[docs/adr/README.md](docs/adr/README.md). Live docs cite the governing
accepted ADR, not a superseded record. Do not delete or move ADR files
([2026-09-18-adr-topic-index.md](docs/adr/2026-09-18-adr-topic-index.md)).
How to tag audit claims: [docs/how-to-audit.md](docs/how-to-audit.md).

This is a NixOS flake for a homelab plus two cloud VMs. GitLab is CI of record
(`docs/adr/2026-08-29-gitlab-ci-of-record.md`). Decisions live in
`docs/adr/README.md`. Service docs: `docs/`. Custom options:
`docs/custom-options.md`.
